UID:10001913-1777204800-1777222800@www.culturelink.ca
SUMMARY:NEATwalks: Downsview Park - Exploring Earth Day Activities
DESCRIPTION:Join CultureLink’s NEATwalks program for a special Earth Day outing at Downsview Park! This slow‑paced\, family‑friendly walk invites newcomers to Canada to explore one of Toronto’s largest urban parks while discovering a variety of interactive Earth Day stations and activities. \nDress for the weather as this is a rain or shine event. Be sure to bring lunch/ snacks and water with you. Please arrive by 12pm. We will be meeting at 70 Canuck Avenue\, North York\, M3K 2C5 near Keele St. and Sheppard Ave. West. \nFor newcomers to Canada (Permanent Residents and Convention Refugees). \nFor new participants fill out this Registration Form. \n﻿﻿  \nFor returning participants please reserve your spot via text to Rubeen at (437) 249-7103 or email at rchauhan@culturelink.ca. \nFunded by Immigration\, Refugees and Citizenship Canada.
URL:https://www.culturelink.ca/event/neatwalks-downsview-park/
CATEGORIES:Adults,Families,Sustainable Communities
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://www.culturelink.ca/wp-content/uploads/2023/08/Adults-Mentorship-and-Networking-CultureLink-Icon.jpg
END:VEVENT
