SUMMARY:Make Your Mark: Volunteer\, Learn\, Grow
DESCRIPTION:Discover how volunteering can open doors to new opportunities and help you build valuable skills for your future. This session will guide you through the benefits of giving back while gaining meaningful experience. \nIn this session participants will: \n\nUnderstand the importance and impact of volunteering in the community\nLearn how to find and apply for volunteer opportunities\nExplore how volunteering can strengthen resumes and support employment goals\nGain tips on how building skills\, confidence and professional networks\n\nTake the first step toward growth- make your mark through volunteering! \nFor Newcomers (Permanent Residents & Convention Refugees). \nFor more information contact Shane at saquino@culutrelink.ca or (416) 931-6536. \nTo register please fill out this Registration Form. \n﻿﻿  \n  \nFunded by Immigration\, Refugees and Citizenship Canada.
URL:https://www.culturelink.ca/event/make-your-mark-volunteer-learn-grow/
LOCATION:Eatonville Library\, 430 Burnhamthorpe Road\, Etobicoke\, Ontario\, Canada
CATEGORIES:Adults
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://www.culturelink.ca/wp-content/uploads/2023/08/Adults-Settlement-CultureLink-Icon.jpg
END:VEVENT
